## Summary
81.7% of integrated care personnel are found to hold concurrent positions with other duties, leading to being overwhelmed by tasks such as issuing seal certificates, processing complaints, and providing integrated care. This highlights significant workload challenges in the integrated care sector.

## Key Points
- 81.7% of integrated care personnel have multiple jobs.
- Duties include civil service tasks like seal certificate issuance and complaint processing.
- Personnel report feeling overwhelmed by the combined workload.
- This situation may affect the efficiency and well-being of care providers.


